.TH ADA-UNLOCKCTL 8 "2026-11-07" "ada-unlock-uefi 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
ada-unlockctl \- apply or remove the ada-unlock UEFI boot application
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ada-unlockctl
.RI { apply | remove | status }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ada-unlockctl
copies the ada-unlock UEFI application and its firmware assets from
.I /usr/lib/ada-unlock/esp
to the mounted EFI System Partition, generates
.I ada-unlock.ini
from
.IR /etc/default/ada-unlock ,
and manages the UEFI boot entry and GRUB kernel command line.
.PP
The UEFI application performs the GPU transaction on the next cold boot, then
chainloads the normal Debian bootloader. It is not run by this command.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Install or refresh the ESP files and the UEFI boot entry, and add or remove the
generated GRUB drop-in according to the current configuration.
.TP
.B remove
Remove the package-managed ESP files, UEFI boot entry, and GRUB drop-in.
Restore the pre-install \fBBootOrder\fP and any ESP files that were overwritten
at install time. This is normally called by the package's
.B prerm
script.
.TP
.B status
Print the current configuration, ESP paths, UEFI entry, boot order, and state
file location without changing anything.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/ada-unlock
Operator configuration. Edit this file and run
.B ada-unlockctl apply
to regenerate the ESP configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/default/grub.d/90-ada-unlock.cfg
Generated GRUB drop-in that appends
.B pci=realloc
when the 64 GiB BAR1 path is selected.
.TP
.I /var/lib/ada-unlock/state
Package-managed state and the pre-install ESP file backups.
.TP
.I /boot/efi/ada-unlock.ini
Configuration read by the UEFI application on the ESP.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR /usr/share/doc/ada-unlock-uefi/README.Debian ,
.IR /usr/share/doc/ada-unlock-uefi/INSTALL.md .
